    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain unobstructed at all times could significantly improve emergency responder entry and exit during an incident. Posting clearly visible address markers at the access road entrance would assist responding units in confirming property identification without delay. The circular driveway configuration may support apparatus staging and turnaround capability, and keeping it free of parked vehicles or equipment would enhance that benefit. The limited rear access near the detached structure is worth communicating to local emergency services in advance, as pre-incident familiarity with that constraint could improve response coordination. Maintaining clearance along the driveway corridor through the dense vegetation would further support responder movement and visibility throughout the property."
